WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.680
A student asked, “What is the meaning of life?”

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:08.820
He answered with a joke: “Your
question has no meaning.”

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:11.720
“Life is like a pendulum.”

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:15.960
“It swings between emptiness and boredom.”

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:18.420
School feels empty. Too much time off gets boring.

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:21.920
Work feels empty. Even karaoke
after work gets boring.

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:25.900
He saw life as a pendulum: emptiness
on one side, boredom on the other.

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:28.940
I would add: when it stops swinging, life ends.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:32.460
But if you discover what life truly means,

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:35.820
you may find truth on one side and life on the other—

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:40.960
and eternity when it stops: a
blessing that lasts forever.

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:45.480
We will come back to that. We can see

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:50.500
how hard philosophers have
searched for life’s meaning.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:55.060
Yet so often the search ends with
more sighs than celebration.

00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:58.840
Some put it with humor, but also with sadness:

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:04.360
“Life, oh life! If it were not dark at both ends,

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:08.980
no one would notice the gray area in between.”

00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:11.900
Do you see? The gray area in between.

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:14.020
Another philosopher put it this way:

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:18.600
“We come into life without a choice.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:23.220
One day, we will lose it
without being able to resist.

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:29.140
Sadder still, so many people live
as if they have no other way.”

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:35.150
If that is all there is, what a bleak view of life.
